                    "text": "Spelling tip: when a name is tricky, use the clear-word alphabet, such as “B for Bravo, C for Charlie.” It sounds professional and it prevents mix-ups. For numbers, say them in single digits, so 452 becomes “four, five, two.”",
                    "underline": false
                }
